    "q-159337": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159337",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0\\,\\text{or}\\,y<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y}{2\\pi }, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge 0 \\\\ {F}_{Y}(y), & x>2,\\,y\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind ${F}_{X}(x),$ the marginal CDF of $X,$ for $0\\le x\\le 2.$",
      "worked_solution": "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=F(x,\\infty )={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }F(x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $0\\le x\\le 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y}{2\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\pi }\\cdot {lim}_{y\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
