    "q-159318": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159318",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & y<0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & y>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are independent continuous random variables with marginal CDFs ${F}_{X}(x)$ and ${F}_{Y}(y),$ respectively, then the corresponding joint CDF of $F(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)={F}_{X}(x)\\cdot {F}_{Y}(y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2,$ the joint CDF for our random variables is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & ={F}_{X}(x)\\cdot {F}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{y}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the joint CDF is\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0\\text{ or }y<0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{32}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,y>2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}{y}^{3}, & x>2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 1, & x>2,\\,y>2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
